## Why This Is Asked
Tests facility with non-trivial bit tricks on 128-bit values, without branches.

## Key Concepts
- Per-byte masking and bit propagation
- Operating on 128-bit lanes with fixed-width shifts
- Constructing and applying 128-bit constants

## Code Example
```cpp
uint128 perByteMSB128(uint128 x) {
  uint128 t = x;
  t |= t >> 1;
  t |= t >> 2;
  t |= t >> 4;
  const uint128 msbMask = 0x80808080808080808080808080808080;
  return t & msbMask;
}
```

